/target
# The root workspace lock is committed for reproducible `--locked` builds, so
# there is deliberately no `Cargo.lock` ignore rule here: an ignored lock file
# can be regenerated without the change ever being staged, silently
# reintroducing dependency drift. `scripts/check-toolchain.sh` fails if any
# required lock file is matched by `.gitignore`.
# Sub-workspace lock files (e.g. contracts/creditra-credit/Cargo.lock) are
# committed too, so no `Cargo.lock` rule appears here either.
**/*.rs.bk
.env
/coverage
test_snapshots/
*.proptest-regressions
*.profraw
**/*.profraw
/docs/superpowers/
/.remember/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
rustup-init.exe
verify_preservation_baseline.exe
verify_preservation_baseline.pdb
*.wasm
.aider*
